## Authentication
Session Token (x-csrftoken) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (2)
- `POST /recaptcha/enterprise/{enterpriseId}` — Verify reCAPTCHA enterprise token.
- `POST /resource/UserRegisterTrackActionResource/update/` — Track user registration actions.

### Data Read (3)
- `GET /` — Fetch the main Pinterest feed.
- `GET /resource/{resourceId}/get/` — Retrieve a specific resource by ID.
- `POST /_/_/storage_report/` — Get storage usage report.

### Data Write (3)
- `POST /_/_/report/string_usage/` — Report string usage statistics.
- `POST /_/_/trace/trace/` — Submit a trace for debugging.
- `POST /resource/{resourceId}/create/` — Create a new resource (e.g., Pin, Board).

### Core API (1)
- `POST /_/graphql/` — Execute a GraphQL query.

